---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TRACED Privacy | Public Breach Archive"
  description="Read the TRACED privacy policy. The site has no analytics, cookies, accounts, or tracking, and password checks happen with client-side hashing and k-anonymity."
  robots="noindex,follow"
>
  <Nav currentPath="/privacy/" />

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="page-head">
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="muted">Last updated October 21, 2026</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose">
        <section>
          <h2>No accounts, cookies or analytics</h2>
          <p>
            TRACED is a static public breach archive. It has no user accounts, sets no tracking cookies, runs no
            analytics and keeps no behavioral profiles. Cloudflare Pages serves the pages as static files.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Password checks</h2>
          <p>
            Password checks use the Have I Been Pwned k-anonymity model. Your browser hashes the password with SHA-1,
            sends only the first five characters of the hash, and receives a list of possible matches. Your device
            makes the final comparison. The full password never leaves your browser.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Data sources</h2>
          <p>
            Case files are built from public Have I Been Pwned breach data. TRACED is not affiliated with Have I Been
            Pwned or Troy Hunt.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Network requests</h2>
          <p>
            A normal page visit requests static files, including breach metadata, from Cloudflare Pages. Fonts are served
            from this site's own domain, so no font requests go to Google. A password check also calls the Pwned
            Passwords range endpoint with the short hash prefix. TRACED adds no marketing pixels, session replay
            tools, advertising tags or custom analytics scripts to any of these requests.
          </p>
          <p>
            Hosting providers can keep their own request logs. TRACED does not control those logs.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Browser storage</h2>
          <p>
            If you choose a light or dark theme or a different font in the Aa menu, TRACED saves that choice in your
            browser's local storage so it applies on your next visit. It stays on your device and is never sent
            anywhere. Clear your site data to remove it.
          </p>
          <p>
            TRACED does not save searches or account profiles. Your browser may keep its own history, autofill entries
            or cached pages. Your browser and device settings control those.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What the archive can't tell you</h2>
          <p>
            Case files describe public breach records, not the status of your accounts. A record shows what kinds of
            data were exposed, when the incident happened and whether passwords were included. It cannot show whether a
            specific email address or account is yours.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions about this site, contact Jonathan R. Reed through
            <a href="https://jonathanrreed.com/contact/" rel="noopener">jonathanrreed.com/contact/</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
